From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anatoliy Shulika <shulikaa@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] devices: add Broadcom BCM4366

The 5 GHz radio of the TP-Link Archer C2300 v1 identifies as a BCM4366
(14e4:4365): brcmfmac selects brcmfmac4366c-pcie firmware for it and the
firmware banner reports "BCM43666/4". Without an entry here iwinfo falls
back to the generic "Generic MAC80211 802.11ac/n" string, which is what
LuCI then shows.

14e4:4365 is one of four device IDs the kernel's brcm80211 documentation
lists for this chip; the BCM4365 uses a separate set (14e4:43ca-43cc).

Signed-off-by: Anatoliy Shulika <shulikaa@icloud.com>
---
--- a/devices.txt
+++ b/devices.txt
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@
 0x14c3 0x7990 0x14C3 0x6639    0      0  "MediaTek" "MT7996E"
 0x14c3 0x7992 0x14c3 0x7992    0      0  "MediaTek" "MT7992E"
+0x14e4 0x4365 0x14e4 0x4365    0      0  "Broadcom" "BCM4366"
 0x14e4 0xaa52 0x14e4 0xaa52    0      0  "Broadcom" "BCM43602"
 0x02d0 0xa9a6 0x0000 0x0000    0      0  "Cypress"  "CYW43455"
 0x02d0 0x4345 0x0000 0x0000    0      0  "Cypress"  "CYW43455"
 0x1ae9 0x0310 0x1ae9 0x0000    0      0  "Wilocity" "Wil6210"
